# --- Corrections (small reading fixes found during #218, listed on #240) ---

# tern (#240): upstream `T ER1 N Z` is the plural; the bird is "turn", with `burn`.
tern T ER1 N

# clique (#240): upstream holds only "kleek". "Click" is said too (Merriam-Webster lists it
# first; ruled 2026-10-13), so it rhymes with `trick` and with `week`.
clique K L IY1 K
clique(1) K L IH1 K

# voyeur, raconteur (#240): upstream ends both in "oor", which the before-r Normalisation
# would score for `cure`; both end in "er", with `fur`.
voyeur V OY2 Y ER1
raconteur R AE2 K AA0 N T ER1
# doer (#240): upstream `D UW1 R` is one syllable, "door"; it is "DOO-er", like `doers`.
doer D UW1 ER0
# yearling: upstream also has `Y IH1 L IH0 NG`, with no r, which scored it for `schilling`
# and made it the example rhyme that led the 2026-11-08 Synthetic Player off key. It is
# "YEER-ling" or "YUR-ling" (Merriam-Webster gives both).
yearling Y IH1 R L IH0 NG
yearling(1) Y ER1 L IH0 NG

# ashram (#240): upstream `AE1 SH R AA0 M` let stress promotion stress the last vowel, so it
# scored for `calm` and `bomb`; it is "AHSH-rum", the last vowel a schwa.
ashram AA1 SH R AH0 M

# subsection, rectangle, bifocal, orgasm (#290): upstream marks the vowel before the final
# "-shun", "-gle", "-cal" and "-zum" unstressed. Each rhymed only because stress promotion
# stressed it in the syllabic consonant rule's reading, which promotion no longer reads.
# Each carries a light stress, so they keep `section`, `angle`, `focal` and `chasm`.
subsection S AH1 B S EH2 K SH AH0 N
rectangle R EH1 K T AE2 NG G AH0 L
bifocal B AY1 F OW2 K AH0 L
orgasm AO1 R G AE2 Z AH0 M

# -ual words (#290, 2026-11-03): the maintainer ruled that every "-ual" word gets one verdict
# for `cool`. An "oo" before "-al" rhymes on UW L only when it carries the word's main stress
# (`dual`, `cruel`, `accrual`, `renewal`, `fuel`); otherwise it does not, as `ritual` does
# not. Upstream marks the "oo" of these with secondary stress (UW2), which scored them for
# `cool` while `annual` and `ritual` were refused. Each "oo" is written UW0 here, and every
# other upstream reading of the word is kept.
actually AE1 K CH UW0 AH0 L IY0
actually(1) AE1 K CH L IY0
actually(2) AE1 K SH AH0 L IY0
contextual K AA2 N T EH1 K S CH UW0 AH0 L
homosexuals HH OW2 M OW0 S EH1 K SH UW0 AH0 L Z
spiritual S P IH1 R IH0 CH UW0 AH0 L
textual T EH1 K S CH UW0 AH0 L
unusual AH0 N Y UW1 ZH UW0 AH0 L
unusual(1) AH0 N Y UW1 ZH W AH0 L
unusually AH0 N Y UW1 ZH UW0 AH0 L IY0
unusually(1) AH0 N Y UW1 ZH W AH0 L IY0

# nares (#240): upstream `N AE1 R Z` is one syllable; it is two, "NAIR-eez".
nares N EH1 R IY0 Z

# amniotic (#240): upstream stresses the first syllable; it is "am-nee-OT-ik", with `hypnotic`.
amniotic AE2 M N IY0 AA1 T IH0 K

# -ity words (#240): CMUdict marks the final "-ty" of these with secondary stress
# (IY2), so each had the bare Rhyme Key IY: `ability` scored for `tree` and was
# refused for `facility`. No English -ity word puts a beat on its "-ty", so the
# final vowel is IY0 on every reading. Three also carried a second upstream
# error, corrected here because this entry replaces the reading: `concavity`
# had AA for AE, and `intrepidity` and `servility` stressed the wrong syllable.
# The other 182 words ending in an IY2 (`company`, `thirty`, adverbs in -ly) are
# not -ity words, and some are said with a real beat (`bumblebee`): see #284.
ability AH0 B IH1 L AH0 T IY0
actuality AE2 K CH UW0 AE1 L AH0 T IY0
